Hello, Robert!

The motherboard is Microstar MS-6176.  It was using BIOS version 1.3, but
I upgraded it to BIOS 1.4 beta2 before I got the fixed table from you.
The new dsdt for BIOS 1.4 beta2 is attached.

The problem with both BIOSes is that the kernel reports the warnings and
the system stays up.  It wasn't fixed in the new BIOS.

I patched the kernel to use the fixed dsdt.  Now there are now warnings,
but the system stays up.  What's interesting, the reset button doesn't
work after that, so I have to power cycle the system.

I'm not sure if it's a good idea to use fixed dsdt from BIOS 1.3 with BIOS
1.4 beta2.  I can downgrade if you want me to.  But I hope you will fix
the new dsdt.

Windows 2000 and Linux 2.4.x with ACPI support can power down the system.

-- 
Regards,
Pavel Roskin
